    "string_literals": [
      "A dismissed Slidable widget is still part of the tree.",
      "DismissiblePane created on a Slidable without a Key.",
      "DrawerMotion only supports children with non-zero flex",
      "Either autoClose or onNotification must be set.",
      "FlexTransition only supports children with non-zero flex",
      "Make sure to implement the onDismissed handle of the ActionPane and to immediately remove the Slidable widget from the application once that handler has fired.",
      "Only children wrapped into Flexible widgets with non-zero flex are supported",
      "The closest Slidable of DismissiblePane has been created without a Key.\nThe key argument must not be null because Slidables are commonly used in lists and removed from the list when dismissed. Without keys, the default behavior is to sync widgets based on their index in the list, which means the item after the dismissed item would be synced with the state of the dismissed item. Using keys causes the widgets to sync according to their keys and avoids this pitfall.",
      "To avoid this problem, set the key of the enclosing Slidable widget.",
